{"name":"Doll House","hex":"#facfc1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"doll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small figure resembling a human being that is used as a toy.","An attractive young woman.\n\n A transgender woman or transfeminine person, especially one that has a highly sexual and feminine personal style.\n A transgender woman or transfeminine person, in general. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Synonym of doll up. (clarification of this definition is needed)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doll"},{"term":"house","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A structure built or serving as an abode of human beings. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An apartment building within a public housing estate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To keep within a structure or container.","To admit to residence; to harbor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house"}],"entries":[{"title":"Doll House (2022 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Doll House is a 2022 Filipino drama film directed by Marla Ancheta and written by Onay Sales, Erwin Blanco and Faye Lorenzo. It stars Baron Geisler, Althea Ruedas and Mary Joy Apostol."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/Doll_House_2022_Netflix_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doll_House_(2022_film)","wikidata":"Q134291498"},{"title":"Dollhouse","blocks":[{"text":"A dollhouse or doll's house is a toy house made in miniature. Since the early 20th century, dollhouses have primarily been the domain of children, but their collection and crafting is also a hobby for many adults. English-speakers in North America commonly use the term dollhouse, but in the United Kingdom and other English-speaking countries the term is doll's house. They are often built to put dolls in."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Doll%27s_house_%28AM_2003.99.12-1%29.jpg/330px-Doll%27s_house_%28AM_2003.99.12-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollhouse","wikidata":"Q1355866"},{"title":"Doll","blocks":[{"text":"A doll is a model typically of a human or humanoid character, often used as a toy for children. Dolls have also been used in traditional religious rituals throughout the world. Traditional dolls made of materials such as clay and wood are found in the Americas, Asia, Africa and Europe. The earliest documented dolls go back to the ancient civilizations of Egypt, Greece, and Rome. They have been made as crude, rudimentary playthings as well as elaborate art. Modern doll manufacturing has its roots in Germany, from the 15th century. With industrialization and new materials such as porcelain and plastic, dolls were increasingly mass-produced. During the 20th century, dolls became increasingly popular as collectibles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Poup%C3%A9e_c_1870.jpg/330px-Poup%C3%A9e_c_1870.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doll","wikidata":"Q168658"},{"title":"House","blocks":[{"text":"A house is a residential building. It may range in complexity from a rudimentary hut to a complex structure of wood, masonry, concrete or other material, outfitted with plumbing, electrical, and heating, ventilation, and air conditioning systems. Houses use a range of different roofing systems to keep precipitation such as rain from getting into the dwelling space. Houses generally have doors or locks to secure the dwelling space and protect its inhabitants and contents from burglars or other trespassers. Most conventional modern houses in Western cultures will contain one or more bedrooms and bathrooms, a kitchen or cooking area, and a living room. A house may have a separate dining room, or the eating area may be integrated into the kitchen or another room. Some large houses in North America have a recreation room. In traditional agriculture-oriented societies, domestic animals such as chickens or larger livestock may share part of the house with humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg/330px-Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House","wikidata":"Q3947"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/DollHouse_Image_1982.jpg/500px-DollHouse_Image_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/DollHouse_Image_1982.jpg/1280px-DollHouse_Image_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/DollHouse_Image_1982.jpg/500px-DollHouse_Image_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Nostell Doll's House in West Yorkshire, England, This one-of-a kind miniature house was handcrafted in the 1730s. As that time, doll's houses were not considered to be toys; rather, they were called \"baby houses\" and used to teach girls how to run a household.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADollHouse_Image_1982.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Bundesarchiv_B_145_Bild-F001941-0004%2C_N%C3%BCrnberg%2C_Germanisches_Nationalmuseum.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_B_145_Bild-F001941-0004%2C_N%C3%BCrnberg%2C_Germanisches_Nationalmuseum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Bundesarchiv_B_145_Bild-F001941-0004%2C_N%C3%BCrnberg%2C_Germanisches_Nationalmuseum.jpg/500px-Bundesa